---
// What the usage data showed before the redesign. Real numbers only, exact dates unknown.
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
---
<figure class="df">
  <div class="df__grid">
    <div class="df__card df__card--wide">
      <p class="df__k"><Icon name="users" size={18} /> Most farms never logged anything</p>
      <div class="df__bars" role="img" aria-label="1,000 farms entered no data; 400 farms did">
        <div class="df__bar df__bar--muted" style="--w: 100%"><b>1,000</b><span>farms entered no data</span></div>
        <div class="df__bar" style="--w: 40%"><b>400</b><span>did</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="df__card">
      <p class="df__k"><Icon name="layers" size={18} /> Logged in bursts</p>
      <p>Big batches entered seconds apart. Farmers wrote things down in the barn and typed them in later.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="df__card">
      <p class="df__k"><Icon name="grid" size={18} /> Tags assigned in bulk</p>
      <p><b class="df__n">574</b> farms kept assigning tags long after setup, many at a time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="df__card df__card--wide">
      <p class="df__k"><Icon name="compass" size={18} /> Two ways in, used equally</p>
      <div class="df__split" role="img" aria-label="Tasks logged: about half from the cow card or lists, half from the Add event button">
        <span style="--w: 51%">From a cow card or list</span>
        <span style="--w: 49%">From the Add event button</span>
      </div>
      <p class="df__sub">So both doors had to lead to the same short flow.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>What the app's usage data showed before the redesign.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .df { display: grid; gap: var(--s-2); margin: 0; }
  .df figcaption { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--ink-3); }
  .df__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s-2); }
  .df__card { display: grid; gap: var(--s-1); align-content: start; padding: var(--s-3); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg); }
  .df__card--wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .df__card p { font-size: var(--fs-small); }
  .df__k { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); font-size: var(--fs-body) !important; }
  .df__k :global(svg) { color: var(--accent); flex: none; }
  .df__n { font-family: 'Satoshi', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--ink); margin-right: 0.15rem; }
  .df__sub { color: var(--ink-3); }

  .df__bars { display: grid; gap: 6px; margin-top: var(--s-1); }
  .df__bar {
    width: var(--w); display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--accent); color: #fff; min-width: max-content;
  }
  .df__bar--muted { background: var(--tint-3); color: var(--ink); }
  .df__bar b { font-family: 'Satoshi', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .df__bar span { font-size: 0.875rem; }

  .df__split { display: flex; gap: 4px; margin-top: var(--s-1); }
  .df__split span {
    flex: 0 0 calc(var(--w) - 2px); padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.875rem;
    background: var(--tint-3); color: var(--ink);
  }
  .df__split span + span { background: var(--tint-1); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .df__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .df__split { flex-direction: column; }
    .df__split span { flex-basis: auto; }
  }
</style>
